---
// privacy.astro - what packwing, the app, and this website do with your data:
// next to nothing. The Mac App Store links here as the app's privacy policy.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';

const pageTitle = 'Privacy — packwing';
const pageDescription =
  'packwing collects no personal data: no analytics, no tracking, no accounts. Your files stay on your computer, and the app connects only where you ask it to.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  path="/privacy"
  keywords="packwing privacy, packwing privacy policy, file archiver privacy"
>
  <section class="section prose-top">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-tag">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="section-title"><span class="text-gradient-white">Your files are yours.</span></h1>
        <p class="section-desc">
          packwing collects no personal data. There are no analytics, no tracking, no ads and no accounts.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy covers packwing, the app, on macOS (from this website or the Mac App Store), Windows and Linux,
          its command line <code>pkw</code>, and this website. packwing is made by HivePaaS.
        </p>

        <h2>Your files</h2>
        <p>
          packwing opens, makes and extracts archives on your computer. What is in your files, their names and their
          passwords never leave it: nothing is uploaded, and nothing about them is sent to us or to anyone else.
        </p>
        <p>
          The audit log, when you or your organization turn it on, is a file on your computer. packwing never sends
          it anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2>When packwing connects to the Internet</h2>
        <p>Only in these cases, and never to send what is in your files:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Looking for updates.</strong> The versions downloaded from this website look once a day, while
            <em>Look for updates once a day</em> is on (Settings › About), for the list of releases on GitHub
            (<code>raw.githubusercontent.com</code>), and download a new version from GitHub only when you say so. The
            request carries packwing's version and nothing about you. The Mac App Store's version never looks: the App
            Store updates it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your storages.</strong> An S3, WebDAV or SFTP storage you add is reached at the address you gave,
            with the credentials you gave. packwing keeps those credentials in your system's keychain, and sends them
            to that server alone.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Enterprise licenses.</strong> When an organization turns on its <code>LicenseRefresh</code> policy,
            packwing asks <code>portal.hivepaas.com</code> once a day for a newer key, sending the current key and
            nothing else. Otherwise a license key is checked on your computer, and nothing about it is sent.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          GitHub, the servers of your storages and our portal see the address your computer connects from, as any
          server does. GitHub's use of it is covered by
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">its privacy statement</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Purchases</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>In the Mac App Store,</strong> Apple handles the purchase, under
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's privacy policy</a>.
            packwing asks the App Store, on your Mac, whether you hold Pro; we receive no personal data from Apple
            about you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>On this website,</strong> checkout is at <code>portal.hivepaas.com</code>, with
            <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Paddle</a> as our
            reseller and merchant of record. Paddle receives what you enter to pay, and we receive what we need to
            issue and renew your license key: your name, email address and what you bought.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          packwing.app sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts. The server that hosts it keeps
          ordinary request logs (the address a request came from, the page and the browser) to keep the site running
          and safe, and does not use them for anything else.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>packwing collects no data from anyone, children included.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, the new one is published on this page, with its date below. packwing is open source:
          what it sends can be checked in <a href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">its code</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="updated">Last updated November 14, 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
